# The URL contract. LegalStep.tsx and TelemetryNotice.tsx hardcode
# www.nojoin.co.uk/docs/TELEMETRY into every released image up to and
# including v2.3.0, so /docs/* can never 404. docs/ is flat (verified), so
# single-segment rules cover every historical URL. Most specific first: the
# first matching rule wins. Fragments need no handling here; the browser
# reattaches them to the redirect target itself.
/docs/                 https://github.com/Valtora/Nojoin/blob/main/docs/README.md   301
/docs                  https://github.com/Valtora/Nojoin/blob/main/docs/README.md   301
/docs/:page.html       https://github.com/Valtora/Nojoin/blob/main/docs/:page.md    301
/docs/:page.md         https://github.com/Valtora/Nojoin/blob/main/docs/:page.md    301
/docs/:page            https://github.com/Valtora/Nojoin/blob/main/docs/:page.md    301
